# Presentation layer

Responsible only for HTTP: routing, validation, request parsing, response
mapping. Never implement business logic or import Prisma here.

- Routes (`routes/<feature>.ts`) export a `create<Feature>Routes(deps)`
  factory that receives use cases via a typed `<Feature>RouteDeps` object
  (see `applications.ts`) — never import concrete use case classes directly,
  only their types, so composition stays the wiring edge.
- Validate every input with `zValidator("json"/"param"/"query", Schema)` from
  `presentation/schemas/<feature>.schema.ts` (Zod). Never trust unvalidated
  `c.req`.
- Read the authenticated user via `c.get("userId")` (set by
  `middleware/auth.ts`), never trust a client-supplied user id in the body.
- Translate not-found/ownership failures by throwing the typed application
  errors — let the shared `handle-error.ts` `onError` handler map them to HTTP
  status codes. Don't `try/catch` and format errors ad hoc inside routes.
- New nested resource routes follow the existing REST nesting pattern:
  `/:applicationId/rounds/:roundId/questions/:questionId`.
